BLOCKS_NE = r'''- **定义 `def:appM-blocks` — 精确投影、块与条件 (NE)** (no tag). Massless setting of §M.5 (DR + $\overline{\rm MS}$, covariant gauge, D-dimensional operator basis: formal tensors with $g^\mu{}_\mu=D$ and $\gamma^{[\mu_1\cdots\mu_r]}$ of every rank). Let $\sum_{d_O\le a}\Delta C_O(q)\tilde G_{[O];\Phi}(p)=O(|q|^{1-a}\ln^k|q|)$ uniformly in $\hat q\in S^3$, each $\Delta C_O$ being $|q|^{2-d_O}$ times a polynomial in $L=\ln(q^2/\mu^2)$. The **exact projections** act on the coefficient side only: (Pr1) $(\mu\nu)$-(anti)symmetrization; (Pr2) the trace/traceless split in $\mu\nu$; (Pr3) projection onto spherical harmonics of degree $\ell$ in $\hat q$ (legitimate because the remainder bound is uniform in $\hat q$); (Pr4) separation of the terms $|q|^{2-d}L^m$, $d\le a$ — afterwards the relation holds **exactly**; (Pr5) at $D=4$, projection of the output tensor onto an O(4)-isotypic type $\rho$ (Schur's lemma: $\Pi_\rho t_O=t_O\Pi^{W_O}_\rho$ for the equivariant contraction $t_O:W_O\to{\rm Out}$ of the $O$-term). A **block** is the set $\mathcal S$ of operators of one dimension $d$ that survive (Pr1)–(Pr5); on a block the relation reads $\sum_{O\in\mathcal S}\Pi_\rho t_O(\tilde G_{[O]})=0$. $\mathcal S$ satisfies **(NE)** if at $D=4$ the map $(t_O)_{O\in\mathcal S}\mapsto\sum_Ot_O(V^{(4)}_O)$ is injective ($V^{(4)}_O$: four-dimensional tree vertices). The **twist-2 blocks** $\mathcal B^\pm_n$ ($n\ge2$) have $d=n+2$ and $\rho=(\frac n2,\frac n2)^\pm$ (rank-$n$ symmetric traceless tensors of either parity; O(4) labels $[n]$ and $[n,1,1]$). The names (Pr1)–(Pr5), (NE) are local to App M. `\uses{def:prelim-qcd, def:dis-twist}`.
- **引理 `lem:appM-ne` — 条件 (NE) 的适用范围** (数学). In the setting of `def:appM-blocks`: (i) in the $(\mu\nu)$-symmetric channel with $d_O\le5$, (NE) holds; (ii) for every twist-2 block $\mathcal B^\pm_n$, $n\ge2$, (NE) holds, and no four-quark operator lies in $\mathcal B^\pm_n$; (iii) (NE) fails in the $(\mu\nu)$-antisymmetric channel at $d_O=5$ (already at tree level: the rank-5 structure $2\gamma^{[\nu l\alpha q\mu]}/q^4$) and in four-quark blocks with $d_O\ge6$ ($\Gamma^{(5)}\cdot\Gamma_{(5)}=+D(D-1)(D-2)(D-3)(D-4)$); there uniqueness at $D=4$ needs an evanescent-operator prescription (`Dugan:1990de`, `Herrlich:1994kh`). `\uses{def:appM-blocks}`. Proof: full — by the second fundamental theorem for O(4) and the basis $\{\gamma^{[r]}\}_{r\le4}$ of Cl(4), an identity valid at $D=4$ but not at formal $D$ is spanned by terms containing an antisymmetrizer over $\ge5$ slots (a Dirac structure of rank $\ge5$ or a Gram/Schouten $\delta^{[a_1..a_5]}_{[b_1..b_5]}$), each slot needing a distinct carrier (a free index, a momentum or a polarization). (i) An antisymmetrized set contains at most one of $\mu,\nu$ and at most one $\hat q$, and at most $d_O-3\le2$ derivative or gauge slots of $O$; so every set has $\le4$ carriers. (ii) *Content:* $O\in\mathcal B^\pm_n$ requires $W_O\supset\rho$, so the maximal number $y(O)$ of mutually symmetrizable free slots is $\ge n$ (Littlewood restriction keeps the first row). *Count:* derivatives and gauge fields give $\le1$ slot each at cost 1, a quark bilinear $\le1$ slot of a symmetric set at cost 3, ghosts and $B$ none; with $b$ bilinears and slot-free cost $\kappa$, $n\le y\le(n+2-3b-\kappa)+b$, so $2b+\kappa\le2$, $b\le1$ (no four-quark operator); for $b=1$, $\kappa=0$ and the Dirac structure has rank $r'\in\{1,3\}$, because its remaining indices can only be filled by $\mu,\nu$ and Dirac structures of rank $\ge5$ with free indices vanish at $D=4$ ($\Lambda^{r'}\mathbb R^4=0$ for $r'\ge5$). *(NE):* the $\rho$-projection replaces the first-row output by a null vector $z$ of degree $n$ (plus two antisymmetrized auxiliary vectors for $[n,1,1]$); a Gram identity needs $\ge n+6$ momentum/polarization carriers and a Dirac-mixed identity $\ge n+3$, against a supply of $\le n+4$ ($b=0$) or $\le n+1$ ($b=1$). (iii) The explicit structures. Checks: `verify/extend/X3-ope/scripts` f6 (tree-level rank-5 structure), f7 ($+D!/(D-5)!$; even/odd-dimensional Clifford facts; the slot count for $n\le12$). A new argument for an expected fact (no novelty marker).'''

UNIQ_NEW = r'''- **引理 `lem:appM-uniqueness` — OPE 系数的唯一性** [R, R_PT]. （$R_{\rm PT}$ …）(a) *Order by order (massive):* if $[\sum_{d_O\le a}\Delta_O(q)\tilde G_{N[O]}(p)]^{(r)}=O(|q|^\varrho\ln^k|q|)$ for all external field types, $p$ in compact sets and all orders $r$, then each $\Delta^{(r)}_O=O(|q|^\varrho\ln^k|q|)$. (b) *Exact (massless), blockwise:* in every block of `def:appM-blocks` that satisfies (NE), two coefficient families giving a remainder $O(|q|^{D-1-a}\ln^k|q|)$ at Euclidean non-exceptional momenta, both $|q|^{D-d_O}$ times polynomials in $\ln(q^2/\mu^2)$ (with $\hat q$-dependent coefficients), have equal projected coefficients at each order; by `lem:appM-ne` this covers the symmetric channel at $d_O\le5$ and all twist-2 blocks, so all twist-2 invariant functions ($C^{(n)}_{L,i}$, $C^{(n)}_{2,i}$ and the axial analogues) are unique for every $n$; in blocks without (NE) (four-quark blocks with $d_O\ge6$; the antisymmetric channel at $d_O=5$) uniqueness at $D=4$ needs an evanescent prescription. (c) *Formal $D$:* at fixed generic $\varepsilon$, for bare functions with formal-$D$ tree vertices, (a) holds without (NE), coefficientwise in the Laurent expansion in $\varepsilon$, and graded-homogeneous coefficients of degree $>\varrho$ vanish. `\uses{def:appM-normal-product, def:appM-blocks, lem:appM-ne}`. Proof: full — (a), (c) induction in $g^2$: at tree level only operators whose fields match the external string contribute, through their vertex polynomials, which are independent as formal-$D$ tensors (at $D=4$ this is (NE)); lower orders are controlled by induction since the matrix elements do not depend on $q$; distinct powers $|q|^{\kappa-2j\varepsilon}$ separate the orders (known in spirit); (b) apply (Pr1)–(Pr5) to the difference of the two expansions, then (a) for each $L^m$ coefficient: $\Delta_O=e^{(D-d_O)L}P(L)$ with $|P(L)|\le Ke^{-(a+1-d_O)L}L^k\to0$ forces $P\equiv0$; for $O^{(n)}_{q,g}$, $W_O=[n]$ is $\rho$-isotypic, so every harmonic component ($\ell\in\{n-2,n,n+2\}$) of $\Delta C_O$ lies in $\mathcal B^+_n$.'''

