REMRED = r'''- **注 `rem:appM-remainder-reduction` — 余项估计化归为零动量匹配估计；唯一性论证的循环性** (no tag). (1) *Circularity:* "a proven momentum-space OPE discharges `asm:appM-remainder` through `lem:appM-uniqueness`" is circular: `lem:appM-uniqueness`(a), applied to $\sum_O(\tilde C_O-C'_O)\tilde G_{N[O]}=\mathcal R'-\tilde N_a$, needs $\tilde N_a$ to be small, which is the assumption itself (slot X3a: not delivered). (2) *Reduction* (written out in the X3 report, Lemma A.7; complete given its premise): in the massive model of §M.2, `asm:appM-remainder` holds per order **iff** there are $p$-independent coefficients $C'_O$ such that every element of the span generated from $\mathcal R'=\tilde G^T-\sum_{d_O\le a}C'_O\tilde G_{N[O]}$ by $\partial_p$, multiplication by $p$ and $m\partial_m$ is bounded by $K|q|^{D-1-a}\ln^k|q|$, per order, uniformly in $\hat q$, for $p$ in compact sets **containing 0** (the estimate (CTp)). Steps: over-subtraction $\partial^\alpha_p\tilde N_{a,\Gamma}(q;0)=0$ for $|\alpha|\le a-\sum_{E(\Gamma)}d_e$ (the maximal AB part is compatible with all forests); the normalization matrix $M_{(E,\alpha),O}=\partial^\alpha_p\tilde G^E_{N[O]}(0)$ is block-injective at order 0; matching $\Delta C=M^{-1}_{\rm sq}(\partial\mathcal R'|_{p=0})$, likewise for $(m\partial_m)^j\Delta C$. This suffices for `thm:appM-scaling`(ii)–(iv) and `cor:appM-coordinate`. No novelty is claimed (zero-momentum normalization of Zimmermann normal products). (3) *Literature:* position-space remainder theorems, as described in the secondary literature (e.g. `Smirnov:1990rz` p. 110), do not supply (CTp); the designated sources `Zimmermann1973` (to be read first), `Anikin:1978tj`, `Zavyalov:1990kv` and `Bergere:1977wz` were not read in full, so `asm:appM-remainder` stays \tagA (open problem, Ch25). (4) The DR route of §M.5 (`prop:dis-ope-euclid`) does not use `asm:appM-remainder`.'''

EUCLID_TARGET = r'''- *Target:* **`prop:dis-ope-euclid`** (Ch7, [A]) — 欧氏非例外动量下 Green 函数的逐图渐近展开: massless QCD ($n_f$ massless quarks, covariant gauges with $\xi$ in a compact set $\Xi\ni1$, DR + $\overline{\rm MS}$, D-dimensional basis including gauge-variant, ghost and evanescent operators), at each order $r$, for Euclidean non-exceptional $(p,q)$ (no proper partial sum of external momenta vanishes), for $A=B=J$ ($D=2$): **(A1)** $\tilde G^T_{JJ;\Phi}-\sum_{d_O\le a}C_O(q;\mu,\xi)\tilde G_{[O];\Phi}=O(|q|^{1-a}\ln^k|q|)$ uniformly in $\hat q$, in compact non-exceptional $p$ and in $\xi$; **(A2)** $C_O=|q|^{2-d_O}\times$ a polynomial of degree $\le r$ in $L=\ln(q^2/\mu^2)$ with covariant coefficients polynomial in $\xi$; **(A3)** $C^{\overline{\rm MS}}=C^{\rm bare}Z^{-1}$ is finite ($C^{\rm bare}_O$: the sum over the hard subgraphs containing both currents of their DR Taylor coefficients, a function of $(q,g_0,\xi_0,\varepsilon)$ only); **(A4)** blockwise uniqueness under (NE) (`lem:appM-uniqueness`(b), `lem:appM-ne`): all twist-2 coefficients are unique for every $n$. *Proof location (sketch with citations):* (A1), (A3) graph by graph and in operator form at each $\xi$, cited: `Smirnov:1990rz` — checked in full text: its theorem (p. 117) is a mixed statement (a distribution in the coordinate variables and a function of non-exceptional Euclidean momenta, in analytic regularization), the DR function form is only asserted (p. 118), and ghosts, gauge-variant bases and composite spectators are not treated —, `Smirnov2002`, `Chetyrkin:1982zq`, `ChetyrkinTkachov1981` ($R^*$ for coefficient functions); infrared finiteness from `Breitenlohner:1976te` Thm 1 (checked: connected graphs whose internal vertices all have IR degree $\ge4$, with fields of IR dimension $\ge1$, have an $\varepsilon\to0$ limit as tempered distributions in all external momenta; covariant-gauge QCD qualifies); uniformity in $\xi$ by Lagrange interpolation (polynomial in $\xi$ at fixed order); for $\Phi\ne\varnothing$ no additive renormalization of $\tilde G^T$ is needed (the only degree-0 local terms $g^{\mu\nu}AA$, $g^{\mu\nu}\bar cc$ violate the contact-free electromagnetic Ward identity for neutral legs); (A2) from the homogeneity of degree $2-d_O-2k\varepsilon$ of the $k$-loop hard part in bare $(g_0,\xi_0)$; (A4) by `lem:appM-uniqueness`(b). BPHZL route (`Lowenstein:1974qt`, `LowensteinZimmermann1975`): convergence known, remainder estimate open; the two schemes differ by finite renormalizations **and** by finite non-invariant counterterms restoring the Slavnov–Taylor identities in BPHZL (`Breitenlohner:1975hg`, `Breitenlohner:1976te`; ERR-M28). The DR route needs no `asm:appM-remainder` (`rem:appM-remainder-reduction`(4)). Status [A] under decision D3, **unchanged after the verification** (S63-1: the cited theorem was checked and its scope falls short of (A1), (A3) as stated; slot X3b not passed); literature status `Collins1984` §12.8 ("proved in a gauge theory the same way"), `IzubuchiEtAl2018` Sec. II ("widely assumed"); pure Yang–Mills `Hollands:2007zg` (not verified), `Frob:2015uqy`, `Frob:2016mzv` (preprint).'''

EXC_OLD = r'''in BPHZL the IR finiteness of zero-momentum gauge-invariant twist-2 insertions in off-shell forward kinematics can be checked at low orders but has no all-order proof; in DR the algebraic identities hold for any momenta but the remainder estimate needs an extension of the asymptotic-expansion theorems. Hence the rigorous perturbative OPE is at Euclidean non-exceptional momenta; the forward on-shell remainder is `asm:appM-forward`, and the hadronic transition is `asm:intro-np-ope`.'''
EXC_NEW = r'''in BPHZL the IR finiteness of zero-momentum gauge-invariant twist-2 insertions in off-shell forward kinematics can be checked at low orders but has no all-order proof; in DR these insertions exist at every order (`prop:appM-zero-momentum-insertion`, [A]), the algebraic identities hold for any momenta, and for forward on-shell partonic amplitudes the analytic step is the per-graph theorem `thm:appM-forward-expansion` (§M.7). Hence the rigorous perturbative OPE with a remainder bound is at Euclidean non-exceptional momenta; the forward on-shell remainder is `asm:appM-forward` (reduced in §M.7 by `cor:appM-forward-ope`, not discharged), and the hadronic transition is `asm:intro-np-ope`.'''

ZMI = r'''- **命题 `prop:appM-zero-momentum-insertion` — 零动量扭度 2 算符插入在维数正规化中的存在性** [A]. For $n\ge2$ the first-order insertion of $\int d^Dx\,O^{(n)}_i(x)$ (zero momentum transfer) into a two-point function of elementary fields exists in DR at every order; for $p^2<0$ it equals $(-p^2)^{a}\sum_kc_k\ln^k(-p^2/\mu^2)$, with $a$ fixed by dimensional analysis. `\uses{def:dis-twist}`. Proof plan: $\lambda\int O^{(n)}$ is an integrated term of IR degree $n+2\ge4$, and so are its $\overline{\rm MS}$ counterterms; all QCD vertices have IR degree 4 and the fields have IR dimension $\ge1$ in every covariant gauge, so `Breitenlohner:1976te` Thm 1 (hypotheses checked in the X3 report) gives a tempered distribution in $p$; on $p^2<0$ it is a function $f(p^2)$, and dimensional analysis with polynomial $\ln\mu$ dependence, $f(\lambda^2s)=\lambda^{2a}\sum_k(\ln\lambda)^kf_k(s)$, forces the stated form. It settles, for off-shell forward two-point functions, the question left open in `rem:appM-exceptional`. **地位与缺口.** [A]: the $\varepsilon$ of `Breitenlohner:1976te` is the damping regulator of that construction, not the dimension shift of DR, and the identification of its limit with the dimensionally regularized $\overline{\rm MS}$ insertion used here rests on the relation between that paper and `Breitenlohner:1975hg`, which the verification did not check; upgrade path to [R, R_PT]: that identification written out, plus a second independent confirmation.'''

LBC = r'''- **引理 `lem:appM-lbc-formal` — 形式维数下逐圈的定域 BRST 上同调** (数学). Rescale all fields, $\tilde\phi=g_0\phi$, so that $S=g_0^{-2}\tilde S[\tilde\phi]$ and the rescaled BRST operator $\tilde s$, the equation-of-motion ideal $\tilde{\mathcal E}$ (generated by $\partial^\alpha\delta S/\delta\phi$) and the gauge-invariant (GI) monomials are $g_0$-independent; a connected hard subgraph with $E$ soft legs and $L$ loops carries $g_0^{2L+E-2}$, so the $L$-loop part has total weight $W=2-2L$ (weight grading = loop grading). Let $V^g$ be the finite-dimensional $\mathbb Q$-space of formal-$D$ polynomials in $\tilde\phi$ of given four-dimensional dimension, ghost number $g$ and tensor type (indices contracted with $g$, $\hat q$ and $\gamma^{[r]}$ of all ranks), $K=\{X\in V^0:\tilde sX\in\tilde{\mathcal E}\}$ and $\mathcal L={\rm GI}+\tilde sV^{-1}+\tilde{\mathcal E}$. Then $K=\mathcal L$, and for $X\in K$ of loop order $L$ the GI part is $\sum_j\gamma_jg_0^{k_j+2L-2}G_j(\phi)$ with non-negative exponents. `\uses{def:appM-alien, thm:appM-local-cohomology}`. Proof: full — $K\supset\mathcal L$ and both are $D$-independent ($\tilde s$ creates no self-contractions); specialization $D\to n$ is injective on $V$ for **even** $n\ge n_0$ (second fundamental theorem for O($n$); the $\gamma^{[r]}$, $r\le n$, are independent; for odd $n$ the top element is central); covariant elements of $\tilde{\mathcal E}$, GI and $\tilde s(\cdot)$ in dimension $n$ are specializations (averaging over Pin($n$), first fundamental theorem); local BRST cohomology in dimension $n$ (`Barnich:2000zw` Thm 7.1, Lemma 8.1, §§8.3, 8.6, valid in any dimension; `Henneaux:1995ex` §3; `Barnich:1999cy` App.) gives $K(n)=\mathcal L(n)$; non-identity colour-singlet GI monomials have $k_j\ge2$ factors $\tilde F,\tilde\psi,\tilde{\bar\psi}$. A new argument for a standard step (no novelty marker).'''

ALIENS_ADD = r''' Precision (verification of R-M24): the explicit forward counterexample of `Collins:1994ee` concerns a BRST-exact alien operator; for equation-of-motion operators the forward on-shell massless case is simply **not covered** by `lem:appM-alien-vanish` — never claim that it fails. For forward on-shell massless parton targets with the physical polarization average, contracted alien **tree** vertices vanish (EOM vertices $\propto p^2,p_a$; $B$ legs $\propto p_a$; no external ghosts) — the step used in `cor:appM-forward-ope`; it says nothing about off-shell or off-forward matrix elements.'''

BRSTOPE = r'''- **假设 `asm:appM-brst-ope` — OPE 的 BRST 结构：带一个复合旁观者的欧氏展开 (Eε)** [\tagA]. Full text in `ASSUMPTIONS.md`. Content (v2.3, after the X3 verification): **(B2) ≡ (Eε)** — in bare DR at fixed generic $\varepsilon$ (any $\xi_0$, $B$ off shell, no $\gamma_5$, D-dimensional algebra), for one composite spectator $Z=s\phi$ ($\phi$ an elementary field) the large-$q$ expansion $\langle\mathcal J(q)\,Z\,\Phi\rangle=\sum_{d_O\le a}C_O\langle O\,Z\,\Phi\rangle+\sum_{O'}C^Z_{O'}(q;p_Z)\langle O'\,\Phi\rangle+\mathcal R'$ holds, with the coefficients $C_O$ of the expansion without $Z$ (`prop:dis-ope-euclid`), **merged coefficients** $C^Z_{O'}$ (hard subgraphs containing the $Z$ vertex) polynomial in $p_Z$, all coefficients graded-homogeneous, and $\mathcal R'=O(|q|^{1-a}\ln^k|q|)$. **(B1)** is retired (the name is not reused): its Ward identities hold exactly in DR and its contact-term clause is not needed. The earlier (B2), without merged terms, is not the correct generalization of the Euclidean expansion: the merged terms turn $sX_d=0$ into $sX_d\in\mathcal E$ (`thm:appM-brst-reduction`). `\uses{def:appM-alien}`.'''

BRSTRED = r'''- **定理 `thm:appM-brst-reduction` — OPE 系数的 BRST 约化** [R, R_cond]. （$R_{\rm cond}$ …）前提：\cref{asm:appM-brst-ope}。（本定理只涉及部分子态。）Bare DR at fixed generic $\varepsilon$, any $\xi_0$, $B$ off shell, no $\gamma_5$, D-dimensional algebra; $X_d\equiv\sum_{d_O=d}C_OO$ with the bare coefficients of `prop:dis-ope-euclid`. (i) $sX_d\in\mathcal E$ (the ideal generated by $\partial^\alpha\delta S/\delta\phi$) for every $d\le a$; (ii) $X_d$ = GI + BRST-exact + EOM, loop by loop, with GI coefficients that are power series in $g_0$; (iii) with the Joglekar–Lee triangularity (`prop:appJ-local-operators`): $X_d=\sum_jc'_j[O^{\rm GI}_j]+$ (aliens) with $c'=cZ_{GG}^{-1}$ finite, and the coefficients of operators outside GI ⊕ aliens vanish; (iv) between physical states only GI operators survive (`lem:appM-alien-vanish`(b)); at twist 2 these are $O^{(n)}_q$, $O^{(n)}_g$ (`lem:dis-twist-classification`). The statement holds identically in $\xi_0$, hence for $\xi_0=Z_3\xi_R$, $\xi_R=1$. `\uses{asm:appM-brst-ope, def:appM-alien, lem:appM-lbc-formal, lem:appM-uniqueness, lem:appM-alien-vanish, prop:appJ-local-operators, lem:dis-twist-classification}`. Proof: full given the premise — (1) the DR Ward identity $\sum_k\epsilon'_k\langle\mathcal J\phi_1\cdots(s\phi_k)\cdots\phi_n\rangle=0$ ($sJ=0$, `thm:prelim-slavnov-taylor`); (2) inserting (Eε), the non-merged parts give $-\sum_OC_O\langle(sO)\Phi\rangle$; (3) by the DR Schwinger–Dyson identity ($\delta^{(D)}(0)=0$; signs checked, 400/400) the merged parts assemble into $\langle\mathbb E(q)\Phi\rangle$, $\mathbb E(q)=-i\sum_{\phi,O'}O'\,C^{s\phi}_{O'}(q;-i\partial)\,\delta_LS/\delta\phi\in\mathcal E$; (4) $\langle[-\sum_OC_O\,sO+\mathbb E]\Phi\rangle=O(|q|^{1-a}\ln^k|q|)$ for all $\Phi$; (5) degree matching with `lem:appM-uniqueness`(c): every coefficient has exponent above $1-a$, so the bracket vanishes identically, $\sum_{d_O=d}C_O\,sO=\mathbb E_{d+1}\in\mathcal E$; (6) `lem:appM-lbc-formal` loop by loop; (7) physical states: EOM operators vanish on shell, BRST-exact ones between physical states (`KugoOjima1979`). The reference's conditional proposition is valid; its error was to call the old (B2) "the direct generalization" of the Euclidean expansion. No novelty is claimed (`Joglekar:1976pe`, read at abstract level). Content grade [A] (through (Eε)).'''

GI_TARGET = r'''- *Target:* **`prop:dis-ope-gi`** (Ch7, [A]; implication [R, R_cond] under `asm:appM-brst-ope`) — 物理矩阵元只需规范不变算符: for $A=J^\mu$, $B=J^\nu$ ($D=2$) and every $d$, $X_d=\sum_{d_O=d}\tilde C_O(q;\mu)O$ satisfies $sX_d\in\mathcal E$ (`thm:appM-brst-reduction`), hence $X_d$ = GI ⊕ BRST-exact ⊕ EOM (`lem:appM-lbc-formal`); between physical states only gauge-invariant operators survive; the twist-2 part is spanned by $O_q^{(n)},O_g^{(n)}$. *Proof plan (full, given (Eε)):* `thm:appM-brst-reduction`(i)–(iv) and `lem:dis-twist-classification`. The earlier plan ($sX_d=0$ from the old (B1)(B2)) is superseded: with the merged terms of (Eε) one obtains $sX_d\in\mathcal E$, and the local BRST cohomology restores the physical conclusion. Literature: `Joglekar:1976eb`, `Joglekar:1976pe` (Joglekar 1977 I, II; read at abstract level, S63-3), `Hollands:2007zg` (pure Yang–Mills; not verified), `Frob:2016mzv` Thm 2 (preprint; BRST Ward identity of OPE coefficients if $H^{1,4}_{E(4)}(\hat s|d)=0$; not verified). Slot X3d: partial (QCD: (B1)(B2) replaced by (Eε) + local cohomology + Joglekar–Lee; pure Yang–Mills not verified).'''

RG_TARGET = r'''- *Target:* **`prop:dis-ope-rg`** (Ch7, [R, R_OPE]) — RG equation of the coefficients, **derived directly from (A3)** (neither uniqueness nor (NE) is needed): for every basis operator, evanescent ones included, $(\mu\partial_\mu+\beta\partial_\alpha+\beta_\xi\partial_\xi)\tilde C_i=\sum_j\tilde C_j\gamma_{ji}$ with $\gamma=-(\hat{\mathcal D}Z)Z^{-1}$, $\hat{\mathcal D}=\mu\partial_\mu+\beta(\alpha,\varepsilon)\partial_\alpha+\beta_\xi\partial_\xi$; for $\Phi=\varnothing$ the identity-operator coefficient obeys this with an inhomogeneous term. *Proof:* full — $\hat{\mathcal D}$ is the total $\mu$-derivative at fixed $(g_0,\xi_0)$, so $\hat{\mathcal D}C^{\rm bare}=0$ and $\hat{\mathcal D}C^{\overline{\rm MS}}=C^{\overline{\rm MS}}\gamma$; $\gamma$ is finite ($\gamma=2\alpha\partial_\alpha Z_1$ plus poles, and a highest pole $\gamma_K\varepsilon^{-K}\ne0$ would contradict `lem:appM-uniqueness`(c)); the $\beta_\xi$ term is needed ($\beta_\xi=\mu\,d\xi_R/d\mu=\frac{\alpha_s}{2\pi}\xi_R[(\frac{13}6-\frac{\xi_R}2)C_A-\frac43T_Fn_f]+O(\alpha_s^2)$; at $\xi_R=1$ in SU(3) it is $\frac{\alpha_s}{2\pi}(5-\frac23n_f)\ne0$). *Twist-2 gauge-invariant form* (the Ch7 statement): at $\xi_R=1$, $(\mu\partial_\mu+\beta\partial_\alpha)C^{\rm GI}_i=\sum_{j\in{\rm GI}}C^{\rm GI}_j(\gamma_{GG})_{ji}$, because the coefficients outside GI ⊕ aliens vanish (`thm:appM-brst-reduction`, through `prop:dis-ope-gi`), $\gamma_{{\rm alien},{\rm GI}}=0$ and $\partial_\xi\gamma_{GG}=0$ (`prop:appJ-local-operators`), and the twist-2 coefficients are $\xi$-independent (forward OPE `cor:appM-forward-ope`, through `prop:dis-ope-forward`: $T^{(j)}_2$ is an on-shell physical amplitude and $A^{(n)}=\sum Z_{GG}\cdot{\rm tree}$ is $\xi$-independent); solution $\tilde C(q;\mu)=\tilde C(q;|q|,\alpha_s(|q|))\,\mathcal P\exp(-\int_\mu^{|q|}\frac{d\mu'}{\mu'}\gamma)$. Dictionary: $\mu\,dA/d\mu=-\gamma A$ ⇔ $dA/d\ln\mu^2=\Gamma A$ with $\gamma=-2\Gamma$ (row 18, VF-CONV-16); C-even/C-odd distinction of the continuations (`rem:pdf-ns-plusminus`, ERR-M10).'''

FWD_BLOCK = r'''- **引理 `lem:appM-forward-forests` — 前向 2-森林与 Symanzik 多项式** [R, R_PT]. （$R_{\rm PT}$ …）（本引理只涉及部分子态。）For a forward Compton graph with external momenta $p$ at $P_1$, $-p$ at $P_2$, $q$ at $J_1$, $-q$ at $J_2\ne J_1$ and $p^2=0$: $\mathcal F=Q^2(\hat F_0+\omega\hat F_1)$ with $\hat F_0=\sum_{T:\,c_q\ne0}\alpha^{E\setminus T}$ and $\hat F_1=-\sum_Tc_pc_q\alpha^{E\setminus T}$ (sums over spanning 2-forests $T$; $c_p,c_q\in\{0,\pm1\}$); every monomial of $\hat F_1$ occurs in $\hat F_0$ and has a coefficient of modulus $\le1$. `\uses{def:dis-compton}`. Proof: full ($-s_T=Q^2(c_q^2-c_pc_q\omega)$ for each 2-forest). Elementary.
- **引理 `lem:appM-newton` — Newton 多面体控制与 Taylor 级数** (数学). Let $\mathcal G_\lambda=\mathcal U+\hat F_0+\lambda\hat F_1$ with $\hat F_1$ dominated by $\hat F_0$ as in `lem:appM-forward-forests`, $P={\rm Newt}(\mathcal U+\hat F_0)$ full-dimensional and $|\lambda|\le r<1$. (a) $\int_{\mathbb R^N_+}\alpha^{s-1}g\,\mathcal G_\lambda^{-c}$ and all Taylor-term integrals (numerator $g\hat F_1^n$, exponent $c+n$) converge on a common open set of exponents; (b) there $I(\lambda)=\sum_n\lambda^nI_n$, absolutely; (c) the candidate poles of the meromorphic continuation are $\lambda$-independent, and $\frac1{n!}\partial^n_\lambda I|_{\lambda=0}=I_n$ after continuation. `\uses{lem:appM-forward-forests}`. Proof: full — the coefficients lie in $|\arg|\le\arcsin r$, so `Schultka:2018nrs` Thm 3.1 applies, and $s+m\in c\,{\rm int}P+nP\subset(c+n)\,{\rm int}P$; $\sum_n|\binom{-c}n|r^n\le(1-r)^{-|c|}$ and $|\hat F_1|\le\mathcal G_0$, then Tonelli–Fubini; on the cubes of a cubical decomposition of the orthant $\mathcal G_\lambda=x^{m_\sigma}(f_{\sigma,0}+\lambda f_{\sigma,1})$ with real part $\ge(1-r)f_{\sigma,0}>0$; Gel'fand–Shilov continuation and the identity theorem. Standard tools.
- **引理 `lem:appM-matroid` — 拟阵形式与维数正规化的可容许性** (数学). Let $G_0=G+e_q$ ($e_q$ joining $J_1$, $J_2$), with $N$ lines and $L$ loops. (a) $\hat F_0=\mathcal U(G/\{J_1{=}J_2\})$ and $\mathcal U(G_0)=x_q\mathcal U(G)+\hat F_0$, so ${\rm Newt}(\mathcal U+\hat F_0)$ is the base polytope of the dual matroid $M^*(G_0)$ (after dropping $x_q=L+1-\sum x_e$); (b) its dimension is $N+1-c(M(G_0))$, so it is full-dimensional iff $G_0$ is loopless and 2-connected; (c) the facet normals are $e_e$ ($d=0$), $-\mathbb 1$ ($d=-(L+1)$), $-\mathbb 1_F$ ($d=-r^*(F)\le-1$) and $\mathbb 1_{E\setminus F'}$ ($d=L+1-r^*(F'\cup e_q)\ge1$), so $d=0$ only for the coordinate facets; (d) for ${\rm Re}\,a_e>0$, polynomial numerators, Tarasov shifts, Taylor terms and all $\omega\in\mathcal C=\mathbb C\setminus((-\infty,-1]\cup[1,\infty))$, the only $D$-independent candidate poles are $a_e\in-\mathbb N_0$. `\uses{lem:appM-forward-forests}`. Proof: full — deletion–contraction; (b)–(d) are the $q$-only generic-Euclidean case of `Schultka:2018nrs` §4 (Def. 4.3, Thm 4.15, Props 4.17, 4.29, 4.31, Cor. 4.18, Thm 4.32), with Whitney's theorem for 2-connectivity; see also `Borinsky:2020rqs` Thm 32 and `Arkani-Hamed:2022cqe`; the coefficient condition holds for all $\omega\in\mathcal C$ because $1=\frac{(1+\omega)+(1-\omega)}2$. Checks: X3 scripts f1, f3 (21 + 1028 graphs, 0 failures). Known in substance.
- **定理 `thm:appM-forward-expansion` — 前向在壳 DR 振幅的逐图展开定理** [R, R_PT]. （$R_{\rm PT}$：逐图、逐阶严格。）（本定理只涉及部分子态。）Let $\Gamma$ be a connected graph of the amputated forward Compton amplitude of a massless on-shell parton ($p^2=0$) with two current insertions, in dimensional plus analytic regularization (line powers $a_e$). Bridges carrying $\pm p$ are external-leg corrections (removed by amputation; the DR LSZ factor is 1); zero-momentum bridges are gluons whose non-target side carries a single adjoint index, so they vanish by colour graph by graph; bridges carrying $\pm q$ cannot occur. The amplitude is defined by its Lee–Pomeransky/Speer parametric integral at $p^2=0$ (`LeePomeransky2013`): for real $|\omega|<1$ all coefficients are positive and $\mathcal F>0$ on the orthant, so the $(\mathcal F-i0)$ prescription is immaterial and the integral equals the $i\epsilon$ momentum integral; elsewhere it is defined by continuation. Then: **(F1)** for $\omega\in\mathcal C$ the integral converges on an $\omega$-independent open set of regulator values and continues meromorphically with $\omega$-independent candidate poles; every Laurent coefficient (in $\varepsilon$, at $a_e=1$) is holomorphic on $\mathcal C$; **(F2)** for $|\omega|<1$ each Laurent coefficient equals $\sum_n\omega^nI^{[k]}_n$, the sum of the naive Taylor terms (replace $p\to\lambda p$ and expand the integrand in $\lambda$), absolutely and locally uniformly; **(F3)** if $G_0$ is degenerate, both sides vanish. `\uses{def:dis-compton, lem:appM-forward-forests, lem:appM-newton, lem:appM-matroid}`. Proof: full — Tarasov's relation (tensor integrals → scalar integrals in shifted dimensions with shifted powers) and `lem:appM-forward-forests`; for ${\rm Im}\,\omega\ne0$ the coefficients $\{1,1\pm\omega\}$ lie in an open half-plane, so `Schultka:2018nrs` Thm 3.1 applies, with joint holomorphy on the cubes; (F2) by `lem:appM-newton` and the pointwise equality of parametric and momentum-space Taylor terms (Schwinger–Gauss), restricted to DR by `lem:appM-matroid`(d); (F3) by scaling invariance. Checks (X3 scripts): f1/f3, f2 (`ex:appM-forward-triangle`), and the independent reviewer checks rv21_box (box, all powers free), rv2_ladder2 (two-loop ladder), rv32_triangle. **Status (print):** 本书给出的严格证明 of the **analytic step** of the method of projectors. Verified literature: `Larin:1996wd` §2 (checked) applies the projector "to the integrands of all Feynman diagrams", with a remark on the rearrangement of infrared and ultraviolet divergences, and gives no proof of this step; the earlier papers of the method were not checked, and nothing is claimed about their content beyond their use of the method; four reviewer INSPIRE searches found no prior proof. Closest prior result found: `Semenova:2018cwy` §7, Prop. 6, which — like `Jantzen2011` — does not cover this case. The novelty check (Tkachov's papers, `Smirnov2002`, Schultka's §4, `Borinsky:2020rqs`, `Arkani-Hamed:2022cqe`, `NilssonPassare2013`) is open (Ch25), so 「本书新结果」 is **not** printed. The identification of the Taylor coefficients with $\overline{\rm MS}$ OPE coefficients is `cor:appM-forward-ope` ([A]). Slot X3e: PASS per graph; `asm:appM-forward` is only reduced, never 「已解除」.
- **例 `ex:appM-forward-triangle` — 前向三角图：精确的 Taylor 系数** . One-loop forward triangle with free line powers $a_1,a_2,a_3$, $a=\sum_ia_i$: $I=\frac{\Gamma(a-\frac D2)}{\prod_i\Gamma(a_i)}(Q^2)^{\frac D2-a}B(\tfrac D2-a_2,\tfrac D2-a_1-a_3)\,B(a_1,a_3)\,{}_2F_1(a-\tfrac D2,a_1;a_1+a_3;\omega)$; its $\omega^n$ coefficients equal the naive Taylor terms identically in $(a_1,a_2,a_3,D)$; at $a_i=1$ the poles are $-1/((n+1)\varepsilon)$; direct quadrature at six complex $\omega$, four of them outside the unit disk, agrees to $10^{-10}$. `\uses{thm:appM-forward-expansion}`. Checks: X3 scripts f2 (A), rv32_triangle (A, B).
- **例 `ex:appM-forward-nonuniform` — 离壳极限与在壳 DR 值的非一致性** . For the forward triangle at $p^2=-P^2$, $\omega=0$, $D=4$: $Q^2I=\ln(Q^2/P^2)+2+O(P^2\ln P^2)$, whereas the on-shell DR value is a pure pole — the limits $P^2\to0$ and $\varepsilon\to0$ do not commute, which is why `thm:appM-forward-expansion` is stated at $p^2=0$ in DR. `\uses{ex:appM-forward-triangle}`. Check: X3 script f2 (D).
- **引理 `lem:appM-t2-projector` — D 维中 $T_2$ 的投影与前向振幅的全纯性** [R, R_PT]. （$R_{\rm PT}$ …）（本引理只涉及部分子态。）Quark targets are averaged with $\frac12\slashed p$, gluon targets with $d_{ab}/(D-2)$, $d_{ab}=-g_{ab}+(p_aq_b+q_ap_b)/\nu-q^2p_ap_b/\nu^2$ ($d\cdot p=d\cdot q=0$, ${\rm tr}\,d=2-D$). (a) For transverse $T\in{\rm span}\{g,pp,pq,qp,qq\}$: $T_2=\frac{Q^4[(D-1)S_1-(\nu^2/Q^2)S_2]}{(D-2)\nu^3}$ with $S_1=p_\mu p_\nu T^{\mu\nu}$, $S_2=g_{\mu\nu}T^{\mu\nu}$; (b) quark target: each naive term is transverse and of the form $a\nu^ng+b\nu^{n-2}pp+c\nu^{n-1}pq+c'\nu^{n-1}qp+e\nu^nqq$; transversality gives $c=c'=b/Q^2$, $a=eQ^2-b/Q^2$, and the projector returns $b\nu^{n-1}$, so the $\omega^{-3},\dots,\omega^0$ terms cancel for every $n$: $T^{(q)}_2$ is holomorphic on $\mathcal C$, $O(\omega)$, equal to its naive Taylor series, and odd after summing crossed graphs; at tree level in $D$ dimensions $T_2=4\omega/(1-\omega^2)$, $T_1=2\omega^2/(1-\omega^2)$; (c) gluon target: $T=H_0+H_1/\nu+H_2/\nu^2$, with `thm:appM-forward-expansion` applied to each $H_k$: meromorphic on $\mathcal C$, holomorphic on $\mathcal C\setminus\{0\}$, with the naive Laurent expansion; regularity at $\omega=0$ is `cor:appM-forward-ope` ([A]) or `lem:appM-gluon-regularity`. `\uses{thm:appM-forward-expansion, def:dis-compton}`. Proof: full ($S_1=-\frac{\nu^2}{Q^2}T_1+\frac{\nu^3}{Q^4}T_2$, $S_2=-(D-1)T_1+\frac\nu{Q^2}T_2$; first fundamental theorem with $p^2=0$). Checks: X3 scripts f4, rv22 (A, B).
- **推论 `cor:appM-forward-ope` — 每阶的前向在壳部分子 OPE** [A]. (a) For $|\omega|<1$, at every order and Laurent order, $T^{\mu\nu}_j=\sum_OC^{\mu\nu}_O\langle j|[O]|j\rangle$ for an on-shell massless parton target $j$ (physical polarization average); only twist-2 gauge-invariant operators contribute, $A^{(n)}_{i/j}=\sum Z\cdot{\rm tree}$, and $T^{(j)}_2=4\sum_{n\ {\rm even}}\omega^{n-1}\sum_iC^{(n)}_{2,i}A^{(n)}_{i/j}$; $T^{(g)}_2$ is regular at $\omega=0$; (b) for $|q|\ge4p^0$, uniformly in the Euclidean direction, $|T_j-\sum_{d_O\le N}C_O\langle j|[O]|j\rangle|\le C|q|^{1-N}(1+\ln|q|)^k$ — the content of `asm:appM-forward`. `\uses{thm:appM-forward-expansion, lem:appM-matroid, lem:appM-t2-projector, lem:appM-ne, prop:dis-ope-euclid, thm:appM-brst-reduction, prop:appJ-local-operators, lem:appM-alien-vanish}`. Proof plan (full, given the premises): (1) the forward graphs are exactly the hard (AI) two-leg graphs; (2) by `thm:appM-forward-expansion` and `lem:appM-t2-projector` the naive terms sum to $\sum_OC^{\rm bare}_OV_O(p,-p)$, and on-shell bare matrix elements are trees (scaleless loops); (3) $C^{\rm bare}=C^{\overline{\rm MS}}Z$; by `thm:appM-brst-reduction` and Joglekar–Lee the coefficients outside GI ⊕ aliens vanish, GI mixes into GI + aliens and aliens only into aliens; (4) forward on-shell massless trees are built from $p$ alone ($p^2=0$, $\slashed pu=0$, ${\rm tr}(\slashed p\gamma^{[r]})=0$ for $r\ne1$), so they are non-zero only on the $[n]$-isotypic part of dimension $n+2$, i.e. within $\mathcal B^+_n$, where by `lem:appM-ne`(ii) and the Lorentz covariance of $Z$ no evanescent and no four-quark operator occurs — evanescent operators contribute nothing, even through mixing; alien tree vertices contracted with the physical average vanish (`rem:appM-forward-aliens`); (5) gluon regularity: gauge-invariant two-gluon vertices are transverse; (6) with $p^2=0$ only twist 2 survives, with finite coefficients by (A3); (7) the bound (b) from Cauchy estimates on $|\omega|=\frac34$ ($|\omega|\le2p^0/|q|\le\frac12$, $|\hat P|^2_E\le2(p^0)^2$). **地位与缺口.** [A]: through (A3) of `prop:dis-ope-euclid` (cited; [A] by decision D3) and (Eε) of `asm:appM-brst-ope`; `asm:appM-forward` is thereby **reduced** to (A3) + (Eε) + Joglekar–Lee, not discharged, and `prop:dis-ope-forward` stays [A]. One-loop instances: `ex:appM-forward-oneloop` ($N\le8$).
- **假设 `asm:appM-oswi` — 前向在壳胶子振幅的 Ward 恒等式** [\tagA]. Full text in `ASSUMPTIONS.md`. Content: for the amputated forward on-shell gluon Compton amplitude $M_{ab}$ at each order in DR, $p^aM_{ab}\varepsilon^b=0=\varepsilon^aM_{ab}p^b$ for all $\varepsilon$ with $\varepsilon\cdot p=0$ (including $\varepsilon=p$); equivalently $p^aM_{ab}\propto p_b$ (the BRST form, the ghost amplitude being inside the proportionality factor). `\uses{def:dis-compton, def:prelim-brst}`.
- **引理 `lem:appM-gluon-regularity` — 由在壳 Ward 恒等式得到胶子靶在 $\omega=0$ 的正则性** [R, R_cond]. （$R_{\rm cond}$ …）前提：\cref{asm:appM-oswi}。（本引理只涉及部分子态。）The naive Taylor terms of $d^{ab}M_{ab}$ are polynomial in $\omega$; hence $T^{(g)}_2$ is regular at $\omega=0$, without `thm:appM-brst-reduction`. `\uses{asm:appM-oswi, thm:appM-forward-expansion, lem:appM-t2-projector}`. Proof: full — expand the Ward identity termwise (`thm:appM-forward-expansion`(F2)): $p^aM_{n,ab}\varepsilon^b=0$; by the first fundamental theorem $p^aM_{n,ab}=\alpha_np_b$ and $M_{n,ab}p^b=\alpha'_np_a$ with polynomial $\alpha_n,\alpha'_n$; with $p^2=0$, $d^{ab}M_{n,ab}=-g^{ab}M_{n,ab}+\alpha_n+\alpha'_n$, which is transverse (the electromagnetic Ward identity has no contact terms for neutral gluons); apply `lem:appM-t2-projector`(b). Content grade [A]; a new conditional form (the Ward identity at theorem level is open, Ch25).
- **推论 `cor:appM-cut-plane` — 部分子前向振幅在割平面上的全纯性、不连续性与矩** [A]. (a) Quark targets: each Laurent coefficient of $T^{(q)}_2$ is holomorphic on $\mathcal C$ (content [R, R_PT], `lem:appM-t2-projector`); gluon targets: holomorphic on $\mathcal C\setminus\{0\}$ (content [R, R_PT]) and at $\omega=0$ by `cor:appM-forward-ope` ([A]) or `lem:appM-gluon-regularity` ([A] content); (b) ${\rm Disc}\,T^{(j)}_2=4\pi iF^{(j)}_2$ for the Laurent coefficients ([A]: DR cutting rules for Laurent coefficients; a definition if $F_2:={\rm Disc}/4\pi i$); (c) the moment relation $t_n=4\int_0^1x^{n-2}F^{(j)}_2$ for even $n>A+1$, $A$ a fixed-order growth exponent in $\omega$ ([A]: fixed-order growth bounds without fixed poles are open). `\uses{thm:appM-forward-expansion, lem:appM-t2-projector, cor:appM-forward-ope}`. **地位与缺口.** Composite statement; tag = weakest part, [A]: the gluon point $\omega=0$, the DR cutting rules for Laurent coefficients and the fixed-order growth bound. One-loop check: c_dis ($N\le8$). Compare `prop:dis-compton-analytic` (Ch7, IR-regulated targets).'''

