CURVED = r'''- **引理 `lem:appM-curved-approach` — 沿弯曲路径逼近的边界值** (数学). Let $f$ be holomorphic on $X+i(\Gamma\cap B_\gamma)$ ($X\subset\mathbb R^m$ open, $\Gamma\ne\mathbb R^m$ an open convex cone) with $|f(x+iy)|\le C|y|^{-N}$ and distributional boundary value $f_0$; let $\Theta_\eta:X'\Subset X\to\mathbb C^m$ be smooth with ${\rm Im}\,\Theta_\eta\in(\Gamma'\setminus0)\cap B_{\gamma/2}$ for a closed cone $\Gamma'$ with $\Gamma'\setminus0\subset\Gamma$, and $\Theta_\eta\to{\rm id}$ in $C^\infty$ as $\eta\to0$. Then $\int f(\Theta_\eta(x))\varphi(x)\,dx\to\langle f_0,\varphi\rangle$ for $\varphi\in C^\infty_c(X')$. `% uses: none`. Proof: full — a routine extension of the proof of the boundary-value theorem of `Hormander2003` (Thm 3.1.15; 位置待核实 in the reprint): Taylor's formula at $s=1$ for $s\mapsto f(z+isY)$, $Y\in\Gamma$, gives $f=\sum_{k\le N}\frac{(-i)^k}{k!}L^kf_Y+L^{N+1}H$ with $L=Y\cdot\partial_z$ and $H$ continuous up to the edge; $(L^{N+1}H)\circ\Theta_\eta=(a_\eta\cdot\partial_x)^{N+1}(H\circ\Theta_\eta)$ with $a_\eta=(D\Theta_\eta)^{-1}Y\to Y$; integrate by parts; straight approaches identify the limit with $f_0$. Numerical check: X3 script rv32_bv. Standard (proof supplied).'''

POS_OLD = r'''the restriction of four-dimensional distributional boundary values to the one-dimensional slice at fixed $Q^2$ (needed both for positivity and for the edge-of-the-wedge step) is justified by smearing in $Q^2$ (`Epstein1960`; repairs ERR-m24/R5 E9). `\uses{asm:intro-wightman, lem:appM-forward-tube, prop:dis-W-structure}`.'''
POS_NEW = r'''the restriction of four-dimensional distributional boundary values to the one-dimensional slice at fixed $Q^2$ (needed both for positivity and for the edge-of-the-wedge step) is justified for **every** $Q^2>0$: $K$-fold primitives in $w$ ($K>B$) give slice boundary values, weakly continuous in $Q^2$; on test functions supported in the space-like region away from $\mathbf q=0$, SO(3) averaging turns the four-dimensional approach into the curved approach $\Theta_\eta=(x+i\eta,\,s+\eta^2-2ix\eta)$, covered by finitely many patches with fixed closed subcones (`lem:appM-curved-approach`); weak continuity then transfers positivity and support (`Epstein1960` for the one-dimensional edge of the wedge; repairs ERR-m24/R5 E9). `\uses{asm:intro-wightman, lem:appM-forward-tube, prop:dis-W-structure, lem:appM-curved-approach}`.'''

